Amazon S3 folder created for your SageMaker training job:

sagemaker-scikit-learn-2025-05-08-06-53-33-031/

Inside it, there are 3 folders:

| Folder             | Purpose                                                 |
| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| `debug-output/`    | Stores debugging-related output if debugging is enabled |
| `output/`          | Stores the trained model and training output            |
| `profiler-output/` | Stores training performance/profiling information       |

=====

Importance of each folder

1. output/ ⭐

This is the most important folder for you.

output/model.tar.gz

You use this trained model artifact when creating:

SageMaker Model
      ↓
Endpoint Configuration
      ↓
SageMaker Endpoint
      ↓
Insurance Charge Prediction

====
2. debug-output/

Useful mainly when diagnosing training problems.

For a simple project like your Insurance Prediction using Random Forest, you normally do not need to manually handle this folder unless SageMaker debugging is configured.

===

3. profiler-output/

Contains information about training resource usage and performance, such as:

CPU usage
Memory usage
Training bottlenecks
Performance metrics

This becomes more useful for large or slow training jobs.

